course: dictionary
lesson: 8125
title: One word, different jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A repellent is something that pushes away or keeps away. Context tells you which job the word is doing. «Mosquitoes come out in the evening; covering your arms and legs and using repellent keeps them off.» The clue is «keeps them off», so repellent here is something that keeps mosquitoes away.
explain: «A girl in Florida playing outside at dusk puts on long sleeves and insect repellent, because that is when mosquitoes bite most.» Insect repellent is a spray or cream, and insect means a small creature like a mosquito. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
explain: The same word can describe a thing that makes water roll off, as in «water-repellent jacket». It can also be an adjective: «The smell was repellent» means very unpleasant. Look at the words next to repellent to find out which meaning you need.
fact: A repellent keeps animals or insects away, such as insect repellent against mosquitoes.
fact: «Repellent» can also be an adjective meaning very unpleasant or disgusting.
fact: A water-repellent material makes water roll off it instead of soaking in.
fact: Adults should help with insect repellent, keep it away from eyes and mouth, and wash hands after using it.
fact: Repel also means to push away, as magnets repel each other.
exercise: «Mosquitoes come out in the evening; covering your arms and legs and using repellent keeps them off.» What does repellent do here? | It bites the mosquitoes | It makes the evening darker | *It keeps mosquitoes away | It makes mosquitoes hungry
exercise: A «water-repellent jacket» is useful because it does what to water? | *It makes the water roll off | It makes the water warm | It soaks the water up | It turns the water into ice
exercise: Which phrase names a spray that keeps insects away? | *insect repellent | long sleeves | dusk | water-repellent jacket
test: «Cover your arms and legs and use repellent in the evening, because mosquito bites itch.» Which is the best advice about using repellent? | *Keep it away from eyes and mouth, and wash your hands after | Use it only when you are asleep | Put it in your eyes so you can see better | Eat it before a long walk
test: Why does the girl in Florida use insect repellent at dusk? | *Because that is when mosquitoes bite most | Because repellent is a sweet drink | It is a hot evening | It makes her hair shine
exam: In the sentence «The smell from the bin was repellent», what does repellent mean? | *Very unpleasant | Very quiet | Very wet | Very pleasant
